{
  "note": "The demo Digibox's line-up and its day of listings. THE FORMAT is measured end to end against the running box; THE CHANNELS AND PROGRAMMES ARE INVENTED. The authentic 1998 London line-up and its schedules are the listings-reconstruction phase's work, from scanned magazines with provenance, and this file is the shape that work will deliver. Channel numbers are sequential on purpose so nobody reads them as historical.",
  "fields": {
    "serviceId": "DVB service_id. The NIT, SDT and BAT all declare it, so the tables agree.",
    "listingsRef": "MEASURED load-bearing: the box turns this into the table_id extension it asks its listings with. The per-service listings reference.",
    "channelNumber": "The 12-bit half of the BAT 0xB1 entry's packed field. Its MEANING is not established; sequential on purpose.",
    "startSeconds": "Seconds from midnight. The wire carries start and duration halved, so both must be even.",
    "flags": "The four low bits of the BAT 0xB1 entry's packed field, which the box unpacks into four separate record fields. THEIR MEANING IS NOT ESTABLISHED. 0x5 is the value every probe that got the guide to draw used; the demo page had always left them 0, and its ALL CHANNELS grid listed no channels at all. Carried per channel so the question can be asked by changing a data file rather than by editing the page."
  },
